# The stall in a business jet: entering it, and getting out with least height lost.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# `stall` is the aeroplane own published stall speed with everything down,
# which `sim::approach_speeds` works out on the way to the threshold speed.
# The height allowed in the recovery is against where the recovery began.
#
# **A jet at idle descends while it slows, and the lesson does not pretend
# otherwise.** A light aeroplane decelerates to the stall holding its height;
# a clean jet with the thrust off loses thousands of feet doing the same
# thing, which is why the exercise is flown high. The band on the entry is
# wide enough to allow that descent and narrow enough to catch a wing
# dropping into a spiral, which is what it is there for.
#
# **The stall is called at `stall+25`, not at `stall`.** The figure this
# lesson gets is the published stall speed with everything down, and the
# Learjet is flown clean and high here: at twenty thousand feet it breaks at
# about 119 knots against a published figure of 96. Waiting for 96 means
# waiting for a speed that never comes - she breaks, drops, and accelerates
# away in the descent - and the lesson sat watching an aeroplane fall twenty
# thousand feet without ever calling the stall. The margin is the difference
# between a published low-level figure and where a clean aeroplane at height
# actually gives up.

name Stalls in a business jet
teaches business-jet

stage Entering the stall
do Close the throttles and hold the height as the speed comes back
do Keep the wings level: a wing drop is what you are avoiding
hold position/h-agl-ft start-4000 start+400 Keep the wings level as the speed comes back
until velocities/vc-kts <= stall+25

stage The recovery
do Move the control column forward to unstall the wing
do Full power as the nose comes down, and level the wings
need position/h-agl-ft >= start-600 Recover with the least height you can
until velocities/vc-kts >= stall+35
